I built three week-3 items tonight on `night/2026-11-13`, one commit each, plus a STATE/roadmap commit. Each has its own fast test, and each was reviewed by a subagent and fixed before committing. The locked sanity checks haven't run yet. `night.ps1` runs them after this phase, and they decide whether these items count as done. `test_water.py` (the default-output check) passes.

| Commit | Item | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `bb460e5` | MK/CHelpG charges (`--charges mk\|chelpg`) | Water q(O) is −0.753 with MK, the same as the reference, and −0.749 with CHelpG. |
| `66bffe3` | NCI (`--nci`; `render` draws `nci.png`) | The water dimer shows an H···O lobe at −0.025 a.u.; isolated water shows none. |
| `2f464ce` | Fukui (`--fukui`) | Formaldehyde gives f+ C 0.278 / O 0.274 and f− O 0.434, matching the reference. The solvent path matches direct PySCF PCM runs. |

**What you should know:**
- **Order:** `code.md` says to take the first unchecked roadmap item, so NCI went before def2, not in the order STATE suggested. def2 + ECP is the only week-3 item left.
- **`nci.png` hasn't been looked at.** Viewing it needed a command that isn't allowed at night, so I didn't try another way. Please delete the leftover script `runs/_look_nci.py`.
- **NCI grid is coarse:** the grid size (`GRID`) limits the spacing, and PAM3 will be coarser than the ~0.1 bohr NCIPLOT uses. method.txt says this. The Multiwfn comparison is still a day-session job.
- **Assumed MK radius:** Si and Br have no MK radius in the table, so 2.0 Å is assumed. method.txt says so.

**Changes outside the new features:**
- **`--orbitals` bug fixed:** it was wiping earlier method.txt lines. The review found this.
- **UKS choice:** `scf()` now picks UKS or RKS from the molecule's spin, so the Fukui ions can be doublets. Every caller gets the same choice as before, and `test_uks.py` passes.

**Not done:**
- **No queue jobs:** STATE asked to keep the queue free of PAM3 jobs tonight. Suggested PAM3 validation runs are written under Next in STATE.
- **Uncommitted log and report deletions:** these were already in the working tree when I started (`NIGHT_REPORT.md`, `night/logs/*`, the result JSONs). I left them uncommitted.
